# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI Interview Coach - Environment Variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development and fill in real values.
# Never commit `.env.local` or any file containing real secrets.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Meta Llama API
# Server-side only. Must NOT be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ so it is never
# exposed to the browser bundle. Read by services/llama.ts.
#
# services/llama.ts calls `${LLAMA_BASE_URL}/chat/completions` using an
# OpenAI-compatible request/response shape, so any OpenAI-compatible Llama
# provider works here — for example Groq (https://console.groq.com), which
# hosts Meta Llama models behind an OpenAI-compatible API:
#   LLAMA_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   LLAMA_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#   LLAMA_API_KEY=<your Groq API key>
LLAMA_API_KEY=
LLAMA_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
LLAMA_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# Optional request tuning
LLAMA_MAX_TOKENS=2048
LLAMA_TEMPERATURE=0.7
LLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# App configuration
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=AI Interview Coach
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
